## scales-diy

scales-diy-ask = How to weigh an egg on home-made scales with no weights?
scales-diy-title = Scales of our own
scales-diy-question = We make scales: a 30 cm ruler hung by a thread at its middle, and a yoghurt cup on a thread at each end. The arms are equal, so the ruler stays level when the masses in the cups are equal. But we have no set of weights. How to weigh a hen’s egg?
scales-diy-choices = With things of known mass: sheets of paper and water
scales-diy-choices-2 = No way: without weights the scales only show which is heavier
scales-diy-choices-3 = Not exactly — only by eye, by its size
scales-diy-setup = A 30 cm ruler, thread, two yoghurt cups, plasticine, sheets of A4 office paper (80 g/m²), a 10 mL syringe and a glass of water, a hen’s egg
